      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Grantmaker's Description of How Grants are Used</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE CFO REVIEWS THE CONDITIONS OF THE GRANT TO DETERMINE IF THE FUNDS SHOULD BE RESTRICTED TO PARTICULAR PURPOSES. IF THE DONOR HAS INDICATED THAT THE FUNDS MUST BE DIRECTED TO A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, A RESOURCE CODE IS ASSIGNED TO ALLOW ALL FINANCIAL ACTIVITY RELATED TO THE GRANT TO BE TRACKED IN THE ACCOUNTING SYSTEM. QUARTERLY, THE CFO REVIEWS THE REPORTED USE OF THE GRANT FUNDS TO DETEMINE IF ANY EXPENSES ARE INCONSISTENT WITH THE GRANT'S PURPOSE. IF ANY EXPENSES ARE INCONSISTENT, A JOURNAL IS PREPARED TO REASSIGN THOSE EXPENSES TO AN APPROPRIATE RESOURCE.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
    </IRS990ScheduleI>
    <IRS990ScheduleO documentId="IRS990ScheduleO" softwareId="23017517" softwareVersionNum="2023v6.0">
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 11b</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>PRIOR TO FILING THE ORGANIZATION'S 990 REPORT, A DRAFT COPY OF THE REPORT WAS CIRCULATED TO ALL BOARD MEMBERS FOR THEIR REVIEW AND COMMENT. THE BOARD MEMBERS RECEIVE ALL SCHEDULES AND ATTACHMENTS WITH THE EXCEPTION OF SCHEDULE B, WHERE THE NAME AND ADDRESSES OF INDIVIDUAL DONORS WERE REDACTED PER THE BOARD'S REQUEST.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 12c</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE BOARD HAS ADOPTED A CONFLICT OF INTEREST POLICY. EACH MEMBER IS REQUIRED TO ANNUALLY COMPLETE A QUESTIONNAIRE STATING ANY POTENTIAL CONFLICT OF NTEREST RELATIONSHIPS.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 15a</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE BOARD OF HIGH TECH HIGH HAS ESTABLISHED SPECIFIC POLICIES AND PROCEDURES RELATED TO COMPENSATION OF OFFICERS AND KEY EMPLOYEES EMPLOYED BY THE ORGANIZATION. PER THE POLICY, BEFORE MAKING A CHANGE IN PAY, THE BOARD SOLICITS A STUDY FROM AN INDEPENDENT COMPENSATION CONSULTANT. THE BOARD'S COMPENSATION COMMITTEE MAKES A RECOMMENDATION AFTER REVIEW OF THE STUDY AND ALL BOARD MEMBERS ARE PROVIDED A COPY OF THE CONSULTANT'S ANALYSIS.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section C, Line 19</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>HIGH TECH HIGH FOUNDATION MAKES ITS FORM 990, GOVERNING DOCUMENTS, CONFLICT OF INTEREST POLICY, FINANCIAL STATEMENTS AND OTHER CORPORATE DOCUMENTS AVAILABLE TO THE PUBLIC UPON REQUEST.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
    </IRS990ScheduleO>
